(6442556, 955268, 60173, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Blackbox:</b></div><hr/><i> Gosh, people ask for validation for the craziest, petty reasons: they''re jealous! It ticks me off to no end. This is excellent and straight forward. A powerful scene and perfectly captured. 10. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I requested a validation on this, because the top third of the grass is all cloned. As I stated in my comment below, it looks like there was at least a fence there. It could have been anything though, and the cloning was blatantly obvious unfortunately. A simple fence clone is probably just fine, but what if it had been a bunch of houses in the distance that were removed? What about a road? Bunch of cows? I had to ask, not because I didn''t like it or that I were jealous, but because there was evidence left. If the validation request was actually issued apparently the SC was curious too.<br/> <br/>I''m actually really surprised this cloning came from someone that''s such an excellent editor.</td>', 'Originally posted by Blackbox: Gosh, people ask for validation for the craziest, petty reasons: they''re jealous! It ticks me off to no end. This is excellent and straight forward. A powerful scene and perfectly captured. 10.   I requested a validation on this, because the top third of the grass is all cloned. As I stated in my comment below, it looks like there was at least a fence there. It could have been anything though, and the cloning was blatantly obvious unfortunately. A simple fence clone is probably just fine, but what if it had been a bunch of houses in the distance that were removed? What about a road? Bunch of cows? I had to ask, not because I didn''t like it or that I were jealous, but because there was evidence left. If the validation request was actually issued apparently the SC was curious too. I''m actually really surprised this cloning came from someone that''s such an excellent editor.', '2011-06-13 02:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442558, 955643, 30982, '<td valign="top">Lovely!  Congrats on another top ten!</td>', 'Lovely!  Congrats on another top ten!', '2011-06-13 02:59:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442560, 955475, 28742, '<td valign="top">Hey hey, my my! Beautiful! Congrats.</td>', 'Hey hey, my my! Beautiful! Congrats.', '2011-06-13 03:03:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442561, 955238, 113591, '<td valign="top">8 from me. Just think how much higher it would have been if you added a lot more colour, placed it in the middle, gave it more "pop", sharpen it a lot, and took out the ugly white line. hehe.</td>', '8 from me. Just think how much higher it would have been if you added a lot more colour, placed it in the middle, gave it more "pop", sharpen it a lot, and took out the ugly white line. hehe.', '2011-06-13 03:04:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442564, 955529, 113591, '<td valign="top">7 from me. For one or other obscure reason, the sharpness made me not score it higher. It is an amazingly sharp image. While the scene is definitely not overly busy (i.e. is minimal landscape), my brain still saw it as very busy. Stupid brain. I like the image.</td>', '7 from me. For one or other obscure reason, the sharpness made me not score it higher. It is an amazingly sharp image. While the scene is definitely not overly busy (i.e. is minimal landscape), my brain still saw it as very busy. Stupid brain. I like the image.', '2011-06-13 03:12:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442565, 955585, 113591, '<td valign="top">I think it suited the challenge well. - under-appreciated.<br/></td>', 'I think it suited the challenge well. - under-appreciated.', '2011-06-13 03:14:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442566, 955365, 113591, '<td valign="top">Love the colour and the lines. Such a rich feel to it.</td>', 'Love the colour and the lines. Such a rich feel to it.', '2011-06-13 03:15:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442568, 955560, 113591, '<td valign="top">Wooo Ammie, het jy na Malema geluister toe jy die verwerking gedoen het? Net reg vir ''n Psigologiese wraak-riller voorblad.</td>', 'Wooo Ammie, het jy na Malema geluister toe jy die verwerking gedoen het? Net reg vir ''n Psigologiese wraak-riller voorblad.', '2011-06-13 03:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442570, 955680, 113591, '<td valign="top">Something alien about it. Scary. I like that I don''t like.</td>', 'Something alien about it. Scary. I like that I don''t like.', '2011-06-13 03:24:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442576, 955268, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aliqui:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Blackbox:</b></div><hr/><i> Gosh, people ask for validation for the craziest, petty reasons: they''re jealous! It ticks me off to no end. This is excellent and straight forward. A powerful scene and perfectly captured. 10. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I requested a validation on this, because the top third of the grass is all cloned. As I stated in my comment below, it looks like there was at least a fence there. It could have been anything though, and the cloning was blatantly obvious unfortunately. A simple fence clone is probably just fine, but what if it had been a bunch of houses in the distance that were removed? What about a road? Bunch of cows? I had to ask, not because I didn''t like it or that I were jealous, but because there was evidence left. If the validation request was actually issued apparently the SC was curious too.<br/> <br/>I''m actually really surprised this cloning came from someone that''s such an excellent editor. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Agreed on the sloppy job of cloning.  It was a last minute thing, late at night, and I was too tired to spend too much time on it, so I didn''t even notice I did such a poor job on it, however nothing was removed from the image.  I was fixing something minor in the grass and didn''t even notice how much damage I caused to the image until you brought it to my attention.  The image was called for validation during voting and was validated with no problems, so no fence or any object was removed from the original image.</td>', 'Originally posted by aliqui: Originally posted by Blackbox: Gosh, people ask for validation for the craziest, petty reasons: they''re jealous! It ticks me off to no end. This is excellent and straight forward. A powerful scene and perfectly captured. 10.   I requested a validation on this, because the top third of the grass is all cloned. As I stated in my comment below, it looks like there was at least a fence there. It could have been anything though, and the cloning was blatantly obvious unfortunately. A simple fence clone is probably just fine, but what if it had been a bunch of houses in the distance that were removed? What about a road? Bunch of cows? I had to ask, not because I didn''t like it or that I were jealous, but because there was evidence left. If the validation request was actually issued apparently the SC was curious too. I''m actually really surprised this cloning came from someone that''s such an excellent editor.   Agreed on the sloppy job of cloning.  It was a last minute thing, late at night, and I was too tired to spend too much time on it, so I didn''t even notice I did such a poor job on it, however nothing was removed from the image.  I was fixing something minor in the grass and didn''t even notice how much damage I caused to the image until you brought it to my attention.  The image was called for validation during voting and was validated with no problems, so no fence or any object was removed from the original image.', '2011-06-13 03:44:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6442580, 955406, 3585, '<td valign="top">This image reminds me how so envious I get, during our cold and gray winters, when I see the images of lightly dressed, tanned southern-hemispherers. <br/>I wish you a winter short and mild and kindly winded as well. <br/>I enjoyed Tanguera''s closing metaphor.</td>', 'This image reminds me how so envious I get, during our cold and gray winters, when I see the images of lightly dressed, tanned southern-hemispherers. I wish you a winter short and mild and kindly winded as well. I enjoyed Tanguera''s closing metaphor.', '2011-06-13 03:50:47.000000', NULL, 0);
