(6951521, 955345, 7810, '<td valign="top">I actually love the concept of this shot It would have been more dramatic (i think) if you adjusted your POV<br/>This is the kind of shot where as a photographer you gotta get in the dirt. If you shoot this image again try getting as low to the ground as possible and exploit the horizon line<br/>See if there is a way to get some daylight between the bottom of the branches and the ground<br/>Also, I would suggest you move to the left and compose the image (if possible) in a way that you can eliminate the  distracting little tree.<br/> <br/>The other thing to try is shooting the image in longer light ... I mean later in the day <br/>Or maybe on a day where there is some drama in the sky... Clouds baby!!!<br/> <br/>Just my thoughts BTW i think it should have scored better.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting you have a good eye you just need to tweak the details<br/> <br/>Cole<br/></td>', 'I actually love the concept of this shot It would have been more dramatic (i think) if you adjusted your POVThis is the kind of shot where as a photographer you gotta get in the dirt. If you shoot this image again try getting as low to the ground as possible and exploit the horizon lineSee if there is a way to get some daylight between the bottom of the branches and the groundAlso, I would suggest you move to the left and compose the image (if possible) in a way that you can eliminate the  distracting little tree. The other thing to try is shooting the image in longer light ... I mean later in the day Or maybe on a day where there is some drama in the sky... Clouds baby!!! Just my thoughts BTW i think it should have scored better. Keep shooting you have a good eye you just need to tweak the details Cole', '2013-01-07 17:32:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6993616, 954742, 66267, '<td valign="top">depth of field is perfect</td>', 'depth of field is perfect', '2013-03-07 08:48:10.000000', NULL, 0);
